### =====================================================================
### order-service - ready-to-run requests
###
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Calls the service DIRECTLY on port 8108, so we send the X-User-* / X-Store-Id headers
### ourselves (normally the API gateway adds them from the JWT).
###
### Placing an order needs cart-service, customer-service and store-service; the order only becomes
### CONFIRMED when inventory-service and payment-service are running too (and the connectors are registered).
### Seed data: customer1 (user 4) has a Fresh Mart cart worth 201.00 and a HOME address (id 1, PIN 560038).
### The full flow through the gateway is in e2e/phase7-order-saga.http.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8108
@orderId = {{placed.response.body.$.data.id}}


### 1. CUSTOMER (user 4): place an order from my cart, cash on delivery -> 201 PENDING
# @name placed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "addressId": 1,
  "paymentMethod": "COD",
  "note": "Please ring the bell twice"
}


### 2. (wait) CUSTOMER: my order -> CONFIRMED once stock and payment are settled, with the timeline
# @wait 4
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 3. CUSTOMER: my order history, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?page=0&size=10
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 4. CUSTOMER: placing again with the (now empty) cart -> 409 "Your cart is empty"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "addressId": 1,
  "paymentMethod": "COD"
}


### 5. CUSTOMER: invalid request -> 400 (addressId missing, unknown payment method)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "paymentMethod": "CHEQUE"
}


### 6. CUSTOMER (user 7): someone else's order -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
X-User-Id: 7
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 7. VENDOR (store 1): new orders waiting for me
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders?status=CONFIRMED
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 8. VENDOR (store 2): an order of store 1 -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}
X-User-Id: 6
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 2


### 9. VENDOR (store 1): accept
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/accept
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 10. VENDOR (store 1): accept again -> 400 (ACCEPTED cannot become ACCEPTED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/accept
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 11. VENDOR (store 1): packed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/pack
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 12. VENDOR (store 1): ready for pickup (publishes OrderReadyForPickup with both addresses)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/ready-for-pickup
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 13. ADMIN: orders waiting for a delivery partner
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders?status=READY_FOR_PICKUP
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 14. CUSTOMER: track it - deliveryPartnerName appears once delivery-service assigns a partner
#     (the partner's steps - pick up, deliver - are in delivery-service/http/delivery-service.http)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 15. CUSTOMER: still possible to cancel while it waits for a partner (READY_FOR_PICKUP)
#     Skip this request if you want to follow the order through delivery.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "reason": "Changed my mind"
}


### 16. ADMIN: orders whose delivery failed (stock returned, payment refunded or cancelled)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders?status=DELIVERY_FAILED
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 17. INTERNAL: any order (other services)
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/orders/{{orderId}}


### =====================================================================
### Invoices (Phase 11): a PDF once the store accepted the order. Use an accepted or delivered order in @invoiceOrderId.
### Once the order is paid (online, or COD after delivery) the first download stores the PDF under
### app.invoice.storage-dir (./data/invoices) and later downloads read that file: send 18 twice and the
### log shows "generated and stored" only the first time. Unpaid COD is generated every time, not stored.
### =====================================================================

@invoiceOrderId = 1


### 18. CUSTOMER (user 4): the tax invoice of my order (PDF download)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{invoiceOrderId}}/invoice
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 19. VENDOR (store 1): print the invoice to put in the bag
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{invoiceOrderId}}/invoice
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 20. ADMIN: any order's invoice
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders/{{invoiceOrderId}}/invoice
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 21. CUSTOMER: the invoice of a cancelled or pending order -> 400 (request 1 placed one; it was cancelled in 15)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/invoice
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER
